      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nRefs #9650\n\n`export_model` writes the Ollama `Modelfile` after the merged model and tokenizer are already saved. For templates that use dict-valued slots (chatglm3 and yuan), `template.get_ollama_modelfile` raises `ValueError: Dict is not supported.`, so the export exits with an error and leaves an empty `Modelfile` behind.\n\nThis change renders the Modelfile before opening the file. If rendering raises `ValueError`, it logs a warning and skips the Modelfile, so the export completes with the weights and tokenizer. Templates that can be rendered behave as before. This removes the crash; it does not produce an Ollama Modelfile for chatglm3 or yuan.\n\nNotes for review:\n- The `except` covers any `ValueError` from `get_ollama_modelfile`. Today only the dict-slot path raises it.\n- If `export_dir` already contains a Modelfile, it is left as is.\n- Rendering dict slots for Ollama would be a fuller fix, but it needs a maintainer decision, so this PR only avoids the crash.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the contributor guideline?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n\n## Verification\n\nRun locally on Windows with Python 3.11.9 and transformers 5.8.0. CI runs the tests on ubuntu-latest, windows-latest and macos-latest across Python 3.11, 3.12 and 3.13, plus Ubuntu Python 3.11 legs pinned to transformers 4.55.0 and 4.57.1, and separate GPU and NPU workflows. Those CI jobs have not run on this change.\n\n- New test `test_export_dict_slot_template` fails on the base commit with the `ValueError` and passes with this change. Both export tests also pass with transformers 4.57.1 installed locally. transformers 4.55.0 was not run.\n- `tests/e2e/test_train.py`: the five `test_run_exp` cases also fail on the base commit in this Windows environment. I did not investigate the cause.\n- `pytest tests/ tests_v1/`: every failing or erroring test also fails on the base commit, so there are no new failures.\n- `ruff` 0.15.5 check and format pass on the changed files. The repo-wide ruff run reports one pre-existing lint error and two pre-existing format differences in files this PR does not touch; `make style`, which CI runs first, fixes them.\n- License check, `uv build` and the pre-commit hooks pass on the changed files.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
